/// newspeak-spec.pdf 6.3.2's futures, when an initializer raises: that
/// abandons its clause, and a future that had escaped stays unresolved
/// (docs/design/object-model.md, "A clause abandoned by an exception").
/// `escaped` receives `second`'s future before `first`'s initializer
/// raises, so `second`'s initializer has never run; the first message sent
/// to the future after the clause is abandoned forces it, which runs that
/// initializer then and answers its value.
class Spec632AnAbandonedClause = Object new (
    | public escaped. |
) (
    class Probe keep: holder = Object new (
        || public first = {holder escaped: second. nil zork}. public second = 2 + 1. ||
    ) () : ()
    public main: platform args: arguments = (
        | t = platform transcript. |
        t show: ([Probe keep: self. 'no error'] on: Error do: [:error | error class name]); newLine.
        t show: (escaped + 1) printString; newLine
    )
) : ()
